cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Cite the software snapshot using this metadata and its exact commit or tag.
  Cite the original papers separately when using their methods. This repository
  is research software, not a published validation study of measured fabrics.
type: software
title: Textile Optics Engine
version: 0.3.0
authors:
  - name: Phill-lms
repository-code: https://github.com/Phill-lms/textile-optics-engine
abstract: >-
  An explicit fiber-to-ply-to-yarn-to-woven-fabric research engine with
  versioned geometry, constituent optical spectra, validated local 2D wave
  and ray adapters, reduced quasi-static yarn-height equilibrium, hierarchical
  projected-area and SGGX diagnostics, and multi-material explicit-fiber spectral
  path tracing with CIE observation. Developed under user direction with AI
  assistance. Current examples use synthetic materials and regenerate fibers on
  selected yarn tracks; full rod/contact mechanics, aggregate fabric BSDFs,
  measured-fabric fidelity, and metasurface sensing remain separate research tasks.
keywords:
  - computational imaging
  - textile microgeometry
  - woven fabric
  - fiber scattering
  - optical simulation
  - reduced yarn mechanics
  - spectral rendering
  - reproducible simulation
  - research software
